{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_001's core claim — that the adjudication-ritual 'requires independent counterexamples from distinct artifacts' for promotion to 'sustained' — is an unsupported assertion about the ritual's specification. The target provides no evidence that §11.3 actually imposes a distinct-artifacts requirement; it merely assumes one, then indicts the ritual for violating a standard it may never have established. If the ritual's actual threshold for 'sustained' is two independent critics failing on the same artifact (which is precisely what occurred: SRC_007 and SRC_009 on artifact 0c61961a8085), then the promotion is by-definition correct and the 'false positive' charge collapses. The target argues against a straw-man reconstruction of the ritual rather than its real content.","premise":"The adjudication-ritual §11.3 standard for 'sustained' may legitimately be two independent critic failures on a single artifact, in which case the documented event (SRC_007 + SRC_009 on 0c61961a8085) satisfies the ritual exactly and no overpromotion occurs.","target":"167ab415ec741cb639b0a8339ddc97a55b1ae4850139df722b7c080f89dc4466"}]}